# Full translation keys are aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.<lineKey> (see Hytale I18nModule).
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.root.speaker=Thalen Meadowrun
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.root.body=I'm Thalen. Meadowrun. I manage the animals and the products they provide, including wool, hides, eggs, and meat. However, I can't do any of this work without a proper barn, clean bins, and a farming bench for processing. What I need from you is a dedicated barn setup. Hay in the loft, goods in storage.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.root.hc0=You wanted to talk about a house.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.root.hc1=Your name is on the house's bookshelf. You can move in when you're ready.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.root.hc2=The house is still in progress.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.root.c0=I wanted to check in now that your barn is finished.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.root.c1=The barn is finished. I am here to complete the request.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.root.c2=The barn is still under construction. I wanted to ask where things stand.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.root.c3=I want to help you get a barn. Can we start with the plot and token?
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.root.c4=That is all for now. Goodbye for now.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_quest_barn.speaker=Thalen Meadowrun
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_quest_barn.body=Stake the plot for the barn and once the structure is up and the farming bench is installed, I will organize wool, hides, eggs, and cuts of meat into storage for pickup. 
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_quest_barn.c0=I will get the barn built.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_quest_barn.c1=I am not ready to start that yet.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_accepted.speaker=Thalen Meadowrun
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_accepted.body=Excellent. When the roof is secure and I have a dry place to store feed, I will meet you at the farming bench inside. I will show you how I organize intake and storage for the animals' comfort.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_accepted.c0=Sounds good. I will see you when the barn is ready.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_building.speaker=Thalen Meadowrun
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_building.body=The construction sign still lists materials owed to the site. Please finish the deliveries or let me know if you've changed your mind about it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_building.c0=I need to cancel this build.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_building.c1=I am still building and I will finish the barn.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_abandoned.speaker=Thalen Meadowrun
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_abandoned.body=Fair enough, but without the barn, I cannot supply the town with the goods they need.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_abandoned.c0=All right. Maybe we can try again another time.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_done.speaker=Thalen Meadowrun
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_done.body=Now the animals have shelter, and the bins are labeled to my specifications. If hides or eggs run low in storage, come talk to me at the barn and we will replenish supplies.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_done.c0=Good to hear. Thanks for keeping the animal goods coming.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_house_offer.speaker=Thalen Meadowrun
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_house_offer.body=I love animals, but not enough to sleep next to them. Could you give me the same housing as everyone else? I would prefer a real bed over a borrowed cot or pile of hay.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_house_offer.c0=I will stake the house and get it built.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_house_offer.c1=Another time.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_house_accepted.speaker=Thalen Meadowrun
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_house_accepted.body=When the house is built, register me on the bookshelf, then come find me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_house_accepted.c0=You will hear it from me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_house_remind.speaker=Thalen Meadowrun
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_house_remind.body=Build at your pace. When the frame is complete, put my name on the bookshelf inside, then return here. I will maintain the barn operations while you finish your work.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_house_remind.c0=Understood.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_house_finish.speaker=Thalen Meadowrun
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_house_finish.body=Good. I can leave mud and straw at the barn instead of dragging both into the inn. Tell me if hides or eggs run low.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.thalen_house_finish.c0=Happy you have a dry bed.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.gift.love=This is exactly what the animals and I needed. It saves me a trip I was dreading. Thank you sincerely.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.gift.like=That is a kind gesture. I will put it to use the first chance I get.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.gift.neutral=I will store that for now and find a suitable spot once I assess the week's needs in the pens.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.gift.dislike=I work with fleeces and livestock supplies, so raw ore is not useful to me. A miner would appreciate that more than I can.

aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.fallback=If you need the barn, updates on the animals, or information on animal produts, I'm the one to talk to.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.greeting.0=Hay dust in the light means the loft is ventilating properly. That is a good sign for the herd.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.greeting.1=The troughs were full at dawn. The animals sound content today. Almost polite.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.greeting.2=If you hear stamping, it is usually boredom, not disaster. They just want attention.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.greeting.3=I oiled a squeaky hinge on the barn door. Small adjustments like that can keep the animals happy.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.greeting.4=Mud happens naturally. Wipe what you can before touching the feed bins. Cleanliness matters to them.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.greeting.5=Check the storage bins regularly so nothing gets left outside.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.greeting.6=Happy animals produce quality goods. Understanding what they need and keeping them comfortable is key to a happy farmstead.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.greeting.7=The wind through the slats smells like changing weather. The animals may not like it, but I will keep an eye on them.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.greeting.8=I do not whisper to animals. I listen closely and attend to their needs. There is a difference.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.greeting.9=If you're kind to the animals, they will be kind to you. 
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.hint.love.0=I get most of my hay from the farm, but I can always use more. Shears, too.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.hint.love.1=Quality feed or a solid water bucket are great ways to be helpful around here.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.hint.love.2=I could really go for a hearty meal after this. I wonder what Corin's cooking up today.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.hint.love.3=If you bring quality leather, I can work with it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.hint.love.4=Healthy treats for beasts win more trust than gifts for me. I respect that priority.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.hint.dislike.0=I am not amused by people who cart around animal remains. Don't bring any of that around here.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.hint.dislike.1=Street stones and random scrap make poor gifts for a barn hand. Usefulness comes first.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.hint.dislike.2=If an item belongs in a dungeon, keep it out of the barn.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.hint.dislike.3=Rotten food near animals is dangerous. Do not attempt to leave it near the stalls.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.main_hub.hint.dislike.4=I do not want trinkets that scare livestock. Keep noisy bells and junk away from the pens.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.rep_reward_50.speaker=Thalen Meadowrun
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.rep_reward_100.speaker=Thalen Meadowrun

aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.birthday.greeting=My birthday and the pastures are calm. Good sign, I think.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.gift.love.birthday=It is my birthday and this gift is wonderful. You made my whole day.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.gift.like.birthday=A birthday gift like this. You have good taste.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.gift.neutral.birthday=Thanks. A simple gift on my birthday still means a lot.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_rancher.gift.dislike.birthday=It is my birthday and you brought that. Well. I still appreciate the thought.
